 your first  coffee  yay coffee okay so before we get started  of course  my general disclaimer here that the  information in this video is for  entertainment  and educational purposes only and you  should always  speak to a health care provider about  your unique health care needs  all right so let's get into our  questions dear abby  should i consume protein before or after  a workout  i've heard people saying one or the  other and i'm confused as heck  what should i eat before and after a  workout generally speaking  should be carbs protein fats combination  help okay so great question  so it really depends on how close you're  eating to when you're going to be  working out and  since i'm not a sports dietitian  specialist  i consulted with my colleague chelsea  cross for this one to provide some  feedback  and a bit of practice based evidence so  let's start with  pre-workout snacks now before any kind  of short and fast  hit style cardio heavy workout you're  going to want to focus on  fast acting carbs and a bit of protein  but  something ideally a little lower in  fiber which can cause digestive distress  and may potentially slow down the  delivery of that energy  when you really need it so think like a  banana and maybe a little protein powder  or rice cake with some greek yogurt some  people are  bothered by fat in their pre-workout as  it can  impact digestion and absorption but  others find that they need that staying  power  so this is definitely more of a personal  thing and will really depend on your  specific workout  and your metabolism now for slow  longer steady state cardio like going on  a hike that lasts over an hour  or doing like a heavy strength training  session  you'll want to have a balanced  pre-workout snack so something with some  protein  and some long-lasting complex carbs and  even a bit of fat is okay for some  people  just to help provide that long-lasting  fuel  so this could be some full-fat greek  yogurt with fruit  it could be 